WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.901
-Congratulations. You got
married last September.

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:04.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did. September 3rd.
-Congratulations.

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:06.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
-September 3rd.
-Yeah.

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:06.673 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-And you -- Your wedding

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:09.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
was covered by
Martha Stewart's magazine.

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:10.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was.
It was covered by Martha.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:13.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Here's a beautiful photo
from the wedding.

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:13.713 line:92%
-That's my husband, Bill.

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.048 size:78% position:39%
-But did you know --
Bill is your husband?

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:17.717
But you guys, did you know were
you going to be on the cover?

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.219 size:78% position:39%
Did you know you were
the cover wedding?

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:20.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. We had no idea.
It was, like, such a shock.

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:24.224
We knew that the wedding would
be covered by Martha Weddings.

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:26.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we had no idea
that it would be --

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:28.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is it extra stress
when Martha Stewart

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:30.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
is shooting your wedding?
-Yeah, for sure.

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:35.101
I mean, we were, we were very
stressed about the details.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:36.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the biggest thing
was alcohol.

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:39.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, my dad was like,
"There's not enough alcohol,"

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:40.774 size:84% position:42% line:92%
the day of the wedding.

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:43.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, really?
-He went out that morning,

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:44.544 size:84% position:42% line:92%
drove to New Hampshire,

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:48.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
and bought like...
a lot of alcohol.

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:50.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because you can take it back.
-Yeah.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.451 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-And there's no tax.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:52.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's tax-free.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:54.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm from New Hampshire,
and I'm so proud that that's

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:57.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
what people travel to
our fine state for, yes.

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:59.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that's, I mean,
the biggest draw.

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:00.860 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:03.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, yeah,
we had more than enough.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:06.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think we got like
$6,000 back or something.

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:07.000 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's great.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was, like,
a lot of the wedding budget.

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.136 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-I like that that was --

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:11.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, your father
is comedian Chris Elliott.

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:13.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
How was he? Was he a good
father of the bride?

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:14.541 line:92%
Was he -- But he was nervous?

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:17.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He was very nervous.
But he pulled it together.

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:20.480
He, like, had a really --
He had the perfect speech.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:23.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was both sweet and funny
and his true form,

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was just --
it was really nice.

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:26.419 line:92%
And we danced to Paul Simon.

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:28.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What's that?
-We danced to Paul Simon.

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:30.290
-Oh, you danced to Paul Simon.
That's a good one to dance to.

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, no,
Paul Simon wasn't there.

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:35.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
-His speech was better
than Paul Simon's.

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:36.096 line:92%
-I didn't dance with Paul Simon.

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"He gave a great speech while
I danced with Paul Simon."

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:39.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And then who --

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:42.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you have the reception
at your house?

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was in our backyard.
It was a very --

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:48.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, it was pretty formal
for a backyard wedding.

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:51.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
We had a tent and a band
and stuff.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:53.213 line:92%
And my dad was very sweet.

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:57.317 size:84% position:42%
He gave our neighbors
bottles of booze before

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:58.952 line:92%
just because of the noise.

00:01:58.952 --> 00:01:59.752 line:92%
-Gotcha. That's very smart.

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:02.522
-Yeah, I think he, like, slipped
them, like, $100 bills, too.

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:06.192
-Wow. Your dad ran this wedding
like the way you run,

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:09.028 size:84% position:42%
like, an underground
drinking establishment.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:11.865
And then you, like, grease
the palms of the bootleggers.

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:13.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
It was Prohibition Era.

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.168 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:17.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, yeah, we --
And he invited everyone.

00:02:17.504 --> 00:02:20.006
He invited all of our neighbors
to the wedding.

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:21.608 line:92%
-Did he run that by you first?

00:02:21.608 --> 00:02:24.844
-No, no. God, no. I would
have been like, "What?"

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:25.812 line:92%
-Yeah. Were you like, "What?"

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:27.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you all of a sudden
saw your neighbors,

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:28.515 size:84% position:42% line:92%
like, wandering around?

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:32.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, we did not expect
any neighbor to come.

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was one guy
in a Hawaiian shirt

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:37.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
roaming around our backyard
with, like,

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:39.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
leather, brown sand--
Like flip-flops.

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:43.429
-Gotcha. Yeah, 'cause that
seems like a courtesy invite

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:44.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
more than a real invite.
-Right, right.

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:48.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, you take the hint
with the $100.

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:50.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
Pocket the $100.
-Don't show up.

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:53.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's like,
"Man, $100, a bottle of booze,

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:56.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I get to go get
hors d'oeuvres?!"

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:59.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, he hopped the stone wall
with his --

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:01.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
He had a Bud Light,
but it was, like,

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:05.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
the bottles with,
like, the screw top.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.620
-Oh, right.
-So it wasn't a bottle or a can.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:11.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was, like, one of those,
like, keep-it-cold Bud Lights,

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:12.425 line:92%
but he also had a koozie on it.

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:16.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So that was like
his formal Bud Light.

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:17.931 line:92%
He dressed it up in its koozie.

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:21.067
-Yeah, exactly.
-That's formal wear for a beer.

